WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:20.550
- All right Ishii.

00:00:22.216 --> 00:00:23.336
Ishii where'd you grow up?

00:00:23.336 --> 00:00:24.169
Where are you from originally?

00:00:24.169 --> 00:00:25.540
- Compton, California.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.687
- Compton? And tell me about your family.

00:00:27.687 --> 00:00:30.265
You had both of your parents
when you were growing up?

00:00:30.265 --> 00:00:32.430
- I was raised with my grandmother,

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.363
both my parents are on drugs.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.136
- So mom and dad were
never really in your life?

00:00:38.136 --> 00:00:39.407
- No.

00:00:39.407 --> 00:00:40.753
- And how would you
describe your childhood?

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:42.633
- Loss.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:45.960
- What kind of stuff went on?

00:00:47.831 --> 00:00:52.831
- Life, depression, abuse,
disappointment, failure.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.553
- I mean, when you say what kind of abuse?

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:08.063
- Molestation, physical abuse, abandonment

00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:16.207
- And your grandmother didn't protect you?

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.920
- No, it happened to her too and

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.133
she didn't know how to handle it.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.933
- Was it, who, was it your grandfather?

00:01:29.191 --> 00:01:31.140
- No, two uncles, one molested me

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.603
and the other beat me.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.880
- How far do you go to school?

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.243
- I graduated a year
early from high school.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.770
- And where'd you go from there?

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:45.883
- I went to college,

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.723
I went for nursing.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:55.420
And uh, after that, I got married at 19

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.490
to a truck driver that you used to

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.253
transport drugs for my family.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.570
He grew on me, it was a
must I had to marry him.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:08.493
I married him, It was
abusive relationship.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.550
My whole side of the face got fractured.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:17.390
I have a crooked back
from him, running me over

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:20.833
with a truck.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:28.300
And uh, we got divorced
and I got married again.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.590
It was happy, it was good.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:37.870
First time in my life I
was happy and was loved

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:40.950
and yeah I liked him.

00:02:43.055 --> 00:02:44.280
I was pregnant,

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.263
I had his child and a year later.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.093
I lost my son accidentally smothered him.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.980
I started selling drugs,
our house got raided

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:59.313
and they took my daughter.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.913
I quit my job, I was home.

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:07.403
- How many kids do you have?

00:03:07.403 --> 00:03:08.393
- I just have one.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.510
I designed and printed latex

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.903
and foil balloons back in Walmart.

00:03:20.713 --> 00:03:24.380
And uh, I worked there for 18 years.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:25.840
And after my husband died I,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.490
- So you told me how
many kids do you have?

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:37.510
- Just one, it would have
been three, but it's just one.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:40.780
My daughter was a twin, his name was Sean.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.980
And I didn't even know I was having twins.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:46.010
He hid behind my daughter
and when I gave birth

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:50.860
he had come and uh, he was
here for about three months

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.130
and he passed away.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:54.803
- Sorry.

00:03:55.718 --> 00:03:58.218
- (Inaudible)

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:05.010
I held on, it was just after
my first love passed away

00:04:07.798 --> 00:04:11.253
and his son too , his seed I just lost it.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:15.903
I just went downhill and
I haven't come back up.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:26.590
It's hard cause I'm out here alone.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:31.590
No family, one child, no support system,

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.420
because I'm scared of people

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.183
having hurt you and abuse you.

00:04:39.589 --> 00:04:40.839
It's not just that alone,

00:04:43.078 --> 00:04:45.990
I've been alone going on five years.

00:04:50.003 --> 00:04:54.593
Five years, no contact with
the world, no TV, nothing.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:01.913
- What about your child?

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:04.433
What about your child?

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:06.793
- I just got her back.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.939
She's nine, her name is Syrah

00:05:10.939 --> 00:05:13.339
(inaudible)

00:05:13.339 --> 00:05:15.973
She's wonderful, no matter
what I went through.

00:05:17.351 --> 00:05:20.033
She's, she's a beautiful angel.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.260
Now that I do have her back,

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.713
I'm getting a little bit back focus.

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:31.290
I have a wonderful man in my
life who was helping for me

00:05:34.523 --> 00:05:38.950
and that's really having patience

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:43.480
and trust in God that I
will come out of this.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.030
And I've never had that before.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:51.373
Not to give up on me,
when I gave up on myself.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:58.060
- Anyone in your family,
did they help you?

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:59.110
- I have no family.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:01.273
I'm the only child on my mom's side.

00:06:03.171 --> 00:06:06.250
I'm the sixth child on my dad's side

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.863
the youngest and the only girl.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:13.910
But because I am black, my mom black

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:16.433
and they're Spanish, they don't accept me.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.723
- And are drugs a part
of the picture for you?

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.450
- Yes, It's a norm.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.723
I do methamphetamine.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:36.150
It's a norm for me, but it's been so long

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.843
you don't even work anymore.

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:42.790
Now I just take pain pills

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:48.753
to go to sleep or just
to know my thoughts.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.313
This is not where I want to be.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.787
It's not working from,

00:06:58.511 --> 00:07:01.094
(cries softly)

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:06.370
but I believe in God now and

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.700
things have gotten a little easier.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.870
Me and my daughter is not
on the streets anymore,

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:13.803
she's home.

00:07:17.254 --> 00:07:19.923
I just, I don't know I'm just lost.

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:26.973
I'm just lost.

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:37.470
I've never been so lost in my life.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:42.470
I've always had a plan, a
plan B, back up, something.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.660
- Have you, you've had jobs?

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:47.493
- Yes.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:53.220
For 18 years I designed
balloons and printed them.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:57.743
And for two years, I,
I remodeled Wal marts.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:02.583
Yes. City to city, state to state.

00:08:04.241 --> 00:08:06.177
- And you're not working currently?

00:08:06.177 --> 00:08:10.953
- No, I currently got
laid off seven months ago.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:16.573
And after I got laid off, I
really, really hit rock bottom.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.403
I went into depression,

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:24.490
I had to go to a mental institution.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:25.903
I had to get on meds.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.063
I tried to commit suicide twice.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:45.340
It's just an ugly
situation with depression

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:49.493
and drugs don't help it tends to fight us.

00:08:55.147 --> 00:08:56.397
Intensifies it.

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:09.780
- A lot of these people

00:09:12.149 --> 00:09:13.613
who are on drugs out here in Skid Row,

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.720
really just need some love

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.330
but you have to start with yourself.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:24.163
And I lost that,

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.433
I lost it.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.933
So now that I don't really care for myself

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:39.160
nothing even matters no more.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:41.520
Sometimes not even with my daughter

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.093
because I feel like I'm
failing as a parent,

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.183
I'm failing as a woman.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:54.360
It's hard, It's hard.

00:10:03.079 --> 00:10:04.588
- It's hard to feel better about yourself

00:10:04.588 --> 00:10:06.690
and you had to do better for yourself

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:07.663
when you feel so bad about yourself.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:12.310
- I start believing in God.

00:10:15.477 --> 00:10:17.600
I start believing in God

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.493
and now the drugs don't even get me high.

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:24.340
So that's why I went to pain pills

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:27.310
and now those are not even working.

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:28.690
- But you still need them to feel good.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:32.093
- Yes, yes.

00:10:38.727 --> 00:10:39.560
Yeah.

00:10:43.593 --> 00:10:46.210
- What do you think may have changed your

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:48.390
direction in your life
when you were young?

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:50.350
Like if your parents weren't addicts,

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:52.950
perhaps, that might've been
the biggest thing right?

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.653
- The biggest thing is,

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.140
going through pain and
no one's there for you

00:11:04.253 --> 00:11:06.753
going through something
and no one's there for you

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:10.363
crying out for help and no one comes,

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:14.513
no one comes.

00:11:18.054 --> 00:11:21.760
And it hurts, It hurts
when you love people

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.810
and there for people and
no one's coming for you

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.123
when you cry out for help.

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:44.413
The most uh,

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:52.563
the most pain even the molestation,

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:59.220
is my son, knowing that
he's not here because me

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:06.263
he'd be three on the 16th of this month.

